invariant: INV-22
file: tls.c
catches: rec_loop_test
reason: ch_read answers the peer's close_notify with this side's own, as
  TLS 1.2 required and RFC 9846 section 6.1 dropped. In TRANSPORT=tcp-nonblocking
  that send comes from inside ch_read, which colibri's adapter does not
  expect, so the alert is lost; bin/rec_loop_test counts the send.

--- old
        close_read_side(t);
        return CH_ECLOSED;
--- new
        close_read_side(t);
        (void)tlsi_send_alert(t, 1, ALERT_CLOSE_NOTIFY);
        return CH_ECLOSED;
